@subsection validate.h / valrecord.c

These functions are concerned with validating new records and edited
records against a previously validated database.

@defun validateNewRecord (GNode* newNode, GNode* origNode, RecordType ntype, Database* database, ErrorLog* errorLog) @arrow{} bool
Main entry point for validating new and edited records.  Calls both
@code{validateRecord} and the type specific validation function listed
below.
@end defun

@defun validateRecord (GNode* , Database* , ErrorLog*) @arrow{} bool
Does generic record validation.  Validation that is independent of the
record type, such as ensuring that records that are pointed to actually exist.

This is called by @code{validateNewRecord} for every record.

Should probably be renamed.
@end defun

@defun validateNewPerson (GNode* new, GNode* old, Database* database, ErrorLog* errorLog) @arrow{} bool
Validates a person tree.  If @code{old} is @code{null}, then @code{new}
is a new record, otherwise it is an edit of @code{old}.  If errors
occur, they are logged in @code{errorLog} and @code{false} is
returned.  Otherwise, @code{true} is returned.

This is called by @code{validateNewRecord} when @code{ntype} is @code{GRPerson}.
@end defun

@defun validateNewFamily (GNode* new, GNode* old, Database* database, ErrorLog* errorLog) @arrow{} bool
